= Obtaining the Internship

I first heard about the Google internship pipeline from a friend(Pimyn) who was,
at the time, already interning at Google himself. He sent me a referral
into the *EMEA Software Engineering Internship* cycle and, very kindly, walked me through how to prepare and what to expect — the
shape of the interview loop, the pacing of the timeline, the kinds of
problems to be ready for. With the referral in hand I applied through
the Google Careers portal and went through the standard interview
process: a recruiter screen, two coding interviews focused on data
structures and algorithmic reasoning and problem solving, and a host-matching interview 
in which a manager checked if I was the best candidate for their project.

The team that picked me up was Web Performance - a team that focuses on diagnosing and solving any and all issues (such as delay or jittering) that appear when using chrome. The project involved working specifically on
*Perfetto*, Google's open-source performance analysis stack. I joined
as a *Software Engineering Intern* on the 2#super[nd] of June 2025 and
remained with the team for the full thirteen weeks of the internship,
finishing on the 29#super[th] of August 2025.

